   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 29.32,
   "text": "There is also the trap of success. The outsider became the establishment. He won the 1992 election with about 60% and when the opposition boycotted the parliamentary vote, his party took almost every seat. In 1995, when crowds marched against the new VAT under the cry of Kuo Me Preko, four people were shot dead by unidentified gunmen. He won again in 1996 with 57% against Kuo Fuor's 40% and then crucially he obeyed the two-term limit.",
