  {
   "start": 29.32,
   "end": 51.7,
   "text": "Here is the irony. On the 7th of January 2001, he handed power to John Kuo Fuor, the first peaceful transfer from a sitting government to the opposition in our history. And Kuo Fuor had once served about eight months as a secretary in Rawlings' own first PNDC government, a move Ahwoi says was partly about keeping Nigeria's President Shagari, a friend of Kuo Fuor's, on side for oil.",
